── spec.yaml fragment to enable A2A ──
spec:
  runtime: apptainer
  a2a:
    port: 7901

── (A) Curl the fleet AgentCard ──
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:7901/.well-known/agent.json | jq .
  # → {"name": "fleet", "agents": [{"name": "hello-agent", ...}]}

── (B) Curl a specific agent's card ──
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:7901/v1/agents/hello-agent/.well-known/agent.json | jq .
  # → {"name": "hello-agent", "url": "...", "capabilities": {...}}

── (C) Post a turn (the raw protocol) ──
$ curl -sX POST http://127.0.0.1:7901/v1/turn \
    -H 'content-type: application/json' \
    -d '{"role":"user","content":"Hello via A2A"}'
  # → 202 Accepted, body: {"status": "queued", "turn_id": "..."}
  # → assistant reply appears in session.jsonl

── (D) High-level sac wrapper ──
$ sac peer post-turn hello-agent "Hello via A2A"
$ sac agents tail hello-agent --json -n 5
